## 6. OOP

### Class and Object
```java
public class Student {
    private String name;     // fields
    private int age;

    public Student(String name, int age) {   // constructor
        this.name = name;
        this.age = age;
    }

    public String getName() { return name; } // getter
    public void setName(String name) { this.name = name; }

    public void display() {
        System.out.println(name + " - " + age);
    }
}

Student s = new Student("Asha", 20);
s.display();
```

### Constructors
```java
class Person {
    String name;
    Person() { this("Unknown"); }            // constructor chaining
    Person(String name) { this.name = name; }
}
```

### static
```java
class Counter {
    static int count = 0;        // shared by all objects
    Counter() { count++; }
    static void show() { System.out.println(count); }
    static { System.out.println("static block runs once"); }
}
```

### The 4 Pillars

**1. Encapsulation**: private fields + public getters/setters.

**2. Inheritance** (`extends`)
```java
class Animal {
    void eat() { System.out.println("eating"); }
}
class Dog extends Animal {
    void bark() { System.out.println("barking"); }
}
```
- Java supports single class inheritance (multiple via interfaces).
- `super` calls parent constructor/methods.

**3. Polymorphism**
- *Compile time:* method overloading.
- *Runtime:* method overriding.
```java
class Shape { void draw() { System.out.println("Shape"); } }
class Circle extends Shape {
    @Override void draw() { System.out.println("Circle"); }
}
Shape s = new Circle();   // upcasting
s.draw();                 // prints "Circle"
```

**4. Abstraction**
```java
abstract class Vehicle {
    abstract void start();
    void fuel() { System.out.println("fuel"); }   // concrete method
}
class Car extends Vehicle {
    void start() { System.out.println("Car starts"); }
}
```

### Interface
```java
interface Payment {
    void pay(double amount);                     // abstract
    default void receipt() { System.out.println("Receipt"); } // Java 8
    static void info() { System.out.println("Payment API"); }
}
class UPI implements Payment {
    public void pay(double amount) { System.out.println("Paid " + amount); }
}
```

| Abstract Class | Interface |
|----------------|-----------|
| Can have state (fields), constructors | Only constants, no constructors |
| Single inheritance | Multiple implementation |
| Any access modifiers | Methods public by default |
| "is-a" with shared code | "can-do" capability/contract |

