## 9. Generics

```java
class Box<T> {
    private T value;
    Box(T value) { this.value = value; }
    T get() { return value; }
}
Box<String> b = new Box<>("hi");

// Generic method
static <T> void print(T item) { System.out.println(item); }

// Bounded type
static <T extends Number> double sum(List<T> list) {
    double s = 0;
    for (T n : list) s += n.doubleValue();
    return s;
}
```

### Wildcards
- `List<?>`: unknown type (read only)
- `List<? extends Number>`: upper bound (read / **P**roducer)
- `List<? super Integer>`: lower bound (write / **C**onsumer) → **PECS**

**Type erasure:** generics exist only at compile time; the JVM sees raw types.

