### Method References
```java
list.forEach(System.out::println);       // static/instance of object
list.stream().map(String::toUpperCase);  // instance method of type
Supplier<List<String>> s = ArrayList::new; // constructor
```

### Streams
```java
List<Integer> nums = List.of(1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6);

List<Integer> evenSquares = nums.stream()
    .filter(n -> n % 2 == 0)
    .map(n -> n * n)
    .collect(Collectors.toList());              // [4, 16, 36]

int sum = nums.stream().mapToInt(Integer::intValue).sum();
Optional<Integer> max = nums.stream().max(Integer::compare);
long count = nums.stream().filter(n -> n > 3).count();
boolean any = nums.stream().anyMatch(n -> n > 5);

// Grouping
Map<Boolean, List<Integer>> parts =
    nums.stream().collect(Collectors.partitioningBy(n -> n % 2 == 0));

Map<Integer, List<String>> byLen =
    words.stream().collect(Collectors.groupingBy(String::length));

// Joining
String joined = words.stream().collect(Collectors.joining(", "));

// flatMap
List<String> flat = listOfLists.stream().flatMap(List::stream).toList();

// Sorting, distinct, limit, skip
nums.stream().sorted(Comparator.reverseOrder()).distinct().limit(3).toList();

// Parallel
nums.parallelStream().forEach(System.out::println);
```
- **Intermediate ops** (lazy): `filter, map, flatMap, sorted, distinct, limit, skip, peek`
- **Terminal ops**: `collect, forEach, reduce, count, min, max, anyMatch, findFirst`
- A stream can be used **only once**.

### Optional
```java
Optional<String> opt = Optional.ofNullable(getName());
String v = opt.orElse("default");
opt.ifPresent(System.out::println);
String upper = opt.map(String::toUpperCase).orElseThrow();
```

