## 13. Multithreading and Concurrency

### Creating threads
```java
// 1. Extend Thread
class MyThread extends Thread {
    public void run() { System.out.println("Thread running"); }
}
new MyThread().start();

// 2. Implement Runnable (preferred)
Thread t = new Thread(() -> System.out.println("Runnable"));
t.start();
t.join();      // wait for completion
```

### Thread lifecycle
`NEW → RUNNABLE → (BLOCKED / WAITING / TIMED_WAITING) → TERMINATED`

### Synchronization
```java
class Counter {
    private int count;
    public synchronized void inc() { count++; }          // method lock

    public void inc2() {
        synchronized (this) { count++; }                 // block lock
    }
}
```

### volatile and Atomic
```java
private volatile boolean running = true;   // visibility guarantee (not atomicity)

AtomicInteger ai = new AtomicInteger();
ai.incrementAndGet();                      // lock-free atomic
```

### wait / notify (producer-consumer)
```java
synchronized (lock) {
    while (queue.isEmpty()) lock.wait();
    lock.notifyAll();
}
```

### Deadlock
Occurs when threads hold locks and wait for each other. Avoid with consistent lock ordering, timeouts (`tryLock`), and minimal lock scope.

### ExecutorService (thread pools)
```java
ExecutorService ex = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(4);
Future<Integer> f = ex.submit(() -> 42);
System.out.println(f.get());
ex.shutdown();
```

### CompletableFuture
```java
CompletableFuture<String> cf = CompletableFuture
    .supplyAsync(() -> "Hello")
    .thenApply(s -> s + " World")
    .thenCombine(CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(() -> "!"), String::concat);
System.out.println(cf.join());
```

### Locks and concurrent collections
```java
ReentrantLock lock = new ReentrantLock();
lock.lock();
try { /* critical section */ } finally { lock.unlock(); }

ConcurrentHashMap<String, Integer> chm = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
CopyOnWriteArrayList<String> cow = new CopyOnWriteArrayList<>();
BlockingQueue<Integer> bq = new LinkedBlockingQueue<>();
CountDownLatch latch = new CountDownLatch(3);
```

